hi I'm Alicia Malone and even though I  am alone yep totally single I've watched  a lot of romantic movies so I feel  completely qualified to tell you how to  throw the perfect wedding according to  the movie step 1 choose your wedding  party carefully putting together the  right bridal party can be tricky you  want your groomsmen to be up for some  fun but hopefully not too much fun  as for the bridesmaids try not to choose  a maid of honor who is secretly hatching  a plan to steal your groom step 2 vet  your guests  I know it's your big day and you'll  probably want to invite as many people  as possible but beware not all wedding  guests follow traditional wedding  etiquette which includes not being  obsessed with your new bride and trying  to steal her no matter how sweet it may  seem with a British accent then of  course there are the wedding crashers  they sneak in  eat your food drink your booze and  sleaze onto your guests though within  the context of a movie it actually can  be quite sweet step 3  entertainment at a wedding entertainment  can come in many forms sometimes it's  planned like a rockin band and other  times well not so much be sure that the  person who will be performing the  ceremony can actually pronounce the  ceremony and be sure that the best man  actually has your best interests in mind  of course if all else fails you can say  get and head to the dance floor and  finally step 4 run away  I mean if movies have taught me anything  they've taught me this just run run away  it's not too late or maybe it is perhaps  I'm not actually qualified to be giving  all this advice those are my tips on how  to plan the perfect wedding according to  the movie so just follow them and before  you know it well there's always the  honeymoon  [Music]
 

